# OXYCOK Commerce — Customer Service Attack Model

> Customer service must continuously challenge its own answers, assumptions, evidence, escalation logic, intervention behavior, and operational outcomes.

---

# 1. Core Principle

The customer-service system is not trusted because it sounds helpful.

It must continuously ask:

What could make this answer wrong?

What evidence am I missing?

Could I be looking at the wrong customer?

Could I be looking at the wrong order?

Could the policy have changed?

Could the customer be asking something more serious than I think?

Could the source be stale?

Could I be hallucinating?

Could I be over-escalating?

Could I be under-escalating?

Could I be annoying the customer?

Could I be increasing conversion while hurting retention?

Could I be solving a symptom instead of the underlying business defect?

---

