Goal:

Reduce avoidable support demand.

---

# 24. Error-to-Control Rule

Every serious error should produce:

ERROR RECORD
↓
FAILURE CLASS
↓
ROOT CAUSE
↓
PREVENTION CONTROL
↓
REGRESSION TEST
↓
INDEX UPDATE

---

# 25. External Failure Learning

Customer service should continuously study outside failures:

- chatbot hallucination incidents;
- refund automation failures;
- airline/service bot failures;
- e-commerce support failures;
- privacy breaches;
- escalation failures;
- dark-pattern complaints;
- AI support lawsuits;
- misrouted orders;
- payment disputes.

External failures become internal challengers.

---

# 26. False-Green Detection

Attack the customer-service test suite itself.

Look for:

- mocked success only;
- unreachable assertions;
- hard-coded fixture responses;
- policy test not exercising policy;
- identity test using same customer;
- refund test without side effects;
- stale fixtures;
- ignored errors.

PASS must mean the real invariant was exercised.

